# Change log

Simple list of changes, grouped by day.

## 2026-08-07

- Fixed view scripts (billing, tva, trimester, tasks calendar) closing immediately on error instead of showing what went wrong.
- Fixed a crash in terminal output caused by special characters on Windows.
- Bills now get backed up automatically before every billing run.
- Missing PDF library now shows a clear message instead of crashing.
- Installed missing Python libraries needed for billing and PDF export.
- Fixed a missing setting that was blocking bill generation.
- Moved editable settings (billing range, PDF on/off, etc.) into a separate, easy-to-edit settings file.
- Added Belgium to the list of supported client countries.

## 2026-09-13

- Started building a desktop app window around the tool, so it can be used by clicking buttons instead of running scripts by hand.
- All the report pages (billing, TVA, calendar, etc.) now share the same navigation bar and footer, so you can click between them.
- Added a new home page that lists and links to all the other report pages.
- The app window now actually opens: launching it refreshes the home page and shows it in its own window, no browser tab or command line needed.
- Added an "auto refresh" switch in the top bar: on, each page redoes its calculations before showing; off, it shows what was last computed and only recalculates if nothing was computed yet.
- If a page fails to update, it now shows a red warning banner instead of failing silently.
- Every table column header on every report page can now be clicked to sort the rows by that column, ascending or descending.
- Each table now opens already sorted by its most sensible column, and remembers the last column you sorted by so it opens that way again next time.
- Clicking a tab in the app now prints which page is being regenerated in the terminal, and confirms it succeeded (or shows the error) once done.
- Started work on pulling work days straight from Google Calendar: a new tool reads the calendar and shows a preview table of what it found for a given month (day, project, half/full day), without changing anything yet — writing that data into the calendar files comes next.
- Added a zip button to the top bar to back up the database on demand, without having to run a script by hand.
- The TVA page's monthly table now always shows every month up to the current one, even months with nothing to declare, instead of stopping at the last month that had a payment.
- Fixed the "par trimestre" table headers on the Trimestres page: they now line up with the numbers below them instead of sitting to the left.
- Added a "payée le" column to the invoices table on the Facturation page, showing the date each invoice was actually paid, based on the received transfers.
- The Calendrier page now shows a preview of the current month's Google Calendar events under the day grid, with a guess at which project each one matches, so you can review what would be imported before anything is actually added to the tracked days.
- The invoices table on the Facturation page is now split into two: one for unpaid invoices, one for paid ones, instead of one mixed list.
- The Google Calendar preview on the Calendrier page no longer loads automatically when you open the tab (it could be slow) — it now only fetches when you click the new "Charger l'aperçu" button.
- Calendar events whose title starts with "TVA" are now skipped entirely in the calendar import preview, since those are personal declaration reminders, not work days.
- Calendar events whose title starts with a parenthesis, like "(rdv dentiste)", are now also skipped in the calendar import preview.
- Ignored calendar events (TVA reminders, parenthesis notes) now still show up in the calendar import preview, just grayed out, instead of disappearing from the list.
- The calendar import button now follows whichever month you're currently viewing on the Calendrier page, instead of always fetching the real current month.
- Every month of the current year can now be selected on the Calendrier page, even ones with nothing tracked yet, so the calendar import can be used to fill in a month that has no data at all. A month with nothing declared shows "Aucune tâche déclarée" instead of an empty calendar grid.
- The calendar import now understands named words for a day fraction, not just numbers — "preshot" in a calendar title now always means a full day, matched with confidence instead of a rough guess.
- Merged the date and day-of-week columns into one in the calendar import preview table.
- Off/chômé days are now shown grayed out in the calendar import preview too, so the days actually tied to a project stand out more.
- Added actual import buttons to the calendar import preview: one per row, and one to import everything at once. A day that's genuinely new gets added; a day already recorded the same way is left alone; a day recorded differently turns orange and asks for confirmation before replacing it, and is never touched by the "import everything" button (only handled one by one, on purpose).
- Days added by the calendar import now land in the right chronological spot in the file, instead of always being tacked on at the end.
- Clients and projects can now be given their own color, which is used wherever that client or project already shows up in color (the billing pie chart, the calendar view) instead of an automatically picked one. There's no color picker yet — the color has to be typed in by hand for now.
- After importing something from the calendar, the Calendrier page now redoes its calculations and reloads itself automatically, so the day you just added shows up right away instead of needing a manual refresh.
- Fixed a bug where giving one specific invoice a custom title ("objet") was overwriting that project's name everywhere else too (calendar, other invoices, other months) instead of just on that one invoice.
- The Calendrier page now remembers which month you were looking at and reopens on it, instead of jumping back to the current month every time it reloads (in particular right after importing something from the calendar).
- The calendar import preview now shows how many differences still need attention right above the table, updating live as you resolve them one by one.
- Grayed-out days (ignored reminders, off/chômé) are now hidden by default in the calendar import preview, with a checkbox to show them again.
- Removed the separate "chômé" concept, which duplicated "off" for the same purpose (an unpaid, untracked day). Only "off" is used now, everywhere.
- Added a new "Éditer factures" page where you can change the start/end period of an existing invoice, or add a new invoice to a project, directly from the app.
- Added a "PDF" button at the end of each invoice row on the "Éditer factures" page, so you can generate (or regenerate) that invoice's PDF and have it open right away, without running a full billing export.
- The Virements page now lets you record a newly received transfer, and link an existing transfer to an invoice (or change/remove that link), directly from the app instead of editing the file by hand.
- "Ajouter une facture" is now a round + button fixed in the bottom-right corner of the Éditer factures page, which opens a small popup to fill in the project and dates, instead of a form sitting under each project's table.
- Added a "Supprimer" button to each invoice on the Éditer factures page. It's grayed out and disabled for any invoice that already has a received transfer linked to it, so a paid invoice can't be deleted by mistake.
- Fixed the "Ajouter une facture" popup on the Éditer factures page showing up open by default instead of staying hidden until the + button is clicked.
- The "Ajouter une facture" popup no longer asks which project to add to — it now always adds to whichever project tab you currently have open, shown as a label instead of a dropdown.
- Added a new "Clients" page where you can pick one client at a time (same as picking a project on the other pages) and edit its details (name, address, invoicing name, country, VAT number, color), or add a brand new client, directly from the app.
- The client color field now has an actual color picker next to it, instead of only typing a hex code by hand.
- The client address is now edited as two separate fields (street, city), instead of one field where you had to type the line-break character by hand.
- The client country field now suggests countries by name as you type, instead of expecting you to already know the 2-letter code by heart.
- Leaving a client's color field empty when adding or saving it now automatically picks a color no other client is already using, instead of leaving it uncolored.
